  "notes": "University Park, no formal tracks. The entire CSD department catalog was missing -- added minimal entries in new csd_catalog.json. Real bug avoided: for the 'STAT 200/EDPSY 101/PSYCH 200' statistics item, listed STAT 200 first -- PSYCH 200 has a genuine two-part AND prereq (PSYCH 100 AND MATH 21), and MATH 21 is never scheduled anywhere in this plan, matching the recurring uncompletable-placement-gate pattern fixed for several majors this session; the bulletin itself also recommends STAT 200. Of the 'HDFS 229/249N/315/411/418/432/PSYCH 270/471' required-selection pool, picked HDFS 229 (no prereq, simplest). Of the 'EDPSY 14/PSYCH 261' pool, picked PSYCH 261 (prereq PSYCH 100, already scheduled). Explicitly scheduled ENGL 15 and CAS 100A rather than generic GWS slots, since ENGL 202A/B later needs ENGL 15/30H specifically. Handbook verification pass: no separate CSD undergraduate handbook is publicly published (only an FAQ page) -- but the live bulletin (bulletins.psu.edu, 2026-27 edition) itself links directly to the department's real, live course-suggestion page (hhd.psu.edu/csd/student-support/courses) for every one of this plan's Gen Ed and 'Elective' categories, which previously WAS treated as having 'no fixed codes' -- it does, and it's now wired up. Fixed two real Gen-Ed-slot/label mismatches found by diffing against the live Suggested Academic Plan: Semester 3's item was labeled 'GEN ED (Exploration)' but the real plan has an Inter-Domain course there (swapped to gen_ed: INTER-D); Semester 4's was labeled 'GEN ED (Inter-Domain)' but the real plan has an Exploration course there (swapped to a generic unwired Exploration slot, matching this app's convention for that flexible category elsewhere). Split the two generic 'GEN ED (Natural Sciences)' GN slots into their real, ASHA-accreditation-driven sub-types per the bulletin's own footnote 2 ('ASHA requirements for admission to graduate school in SLP or Audiology require a biological science course and a physical science course') and the course-suggestion page's own GN-Human-Biological (BISC 2/4, BIOL 133/155) vs GN-Physical-Science (CHEM 1/101/130, PHYS 1) lists. Wired all 7 generic 'Elective' slots (one labeled 'CSD 431 recommended') to the course-suggestion page's full real elective list, spanning its Neuroanatomy, Linguistics, Personal/Professional Development, Teaching ELL, ASL, Diversity Studies, Health Equity, Disabilities/Special Education, Counseling, Human Development/Aging, and Health Administration/Communication categories -- CSD 431 is listed first in the pool (matching the plan's own 'recommended' note; the engine's option-ranking already prefers earlier-listed eligible options within the same tier, so this alone achieves the 'recommended' framing without a fixed requirement). Omitted the course-suggestion page's 'CMAS 258N' code (no CMAS catalog exists in this app, and that prefix is a Commonwealth-campus Communication Arts and Sciences designation, not clearly offered at this plan's University Park end campus) -- its cross-listed equivalents HDFS 258N and SOC 258N are kept. BISC 2/4 and LTNST 100 have no locally-scraped catalog file (a scraping gap, not a bulletin/advising-page error) so they're included as unchecked fallback options, same tolerance used elsewhere this session for real-but-uncataloged codes.",
